From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ken Smith <ken@design-nex.us>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 23:11:18 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] output: add virtual monitors

hl.virtual_monitor({ output, count | regions, layout, workspaces }) splits one
output into one to three regions. Each region is an ordinary monitor on a
headless output, sized and placed from the host's mode, scale and position;
the host stays enabled but leaves the layout, wl_output and focus the same way
a mirror does, and is arranged as a whole with its regions following it.

Every region after the first of the first split output owns persistent
workspaces s*100+1 to s*100+N with names 1 to N, so each region has its own
set; the first keeps the ordinary workspaces, so splitting moves nothing.

Off unless experimental:virtual_monitors is set, and HYPRLAND_NO_VIRTUAL_MONITORS
turns it off regardless. A change made with confirm = N reverts after N
seconds unless confirmed. Region descriptions start with "Virtual", and desc:
selectors for the host never match a region.
